WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.440 align:start position:19%
Meet the upside-down jellyfish. Instead
of drifting with the current, it rests

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.960 align:start position:19%
on the ocean floor, bell down and
tentacles up.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:13.800 align:start position:19%
Why? Because it is a farmer.
Inside its tentacles live tiny algae

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:17.040 align:start position:19%
that turn sunlight into food through
photosynthesis.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:20.760 align:start position:19%
The jellyfish flips over so its algae
get maximum sun.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:25.200 align:start position:19%
It literally farms sunshine. And when
danger comes, it pulses its bell and

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:28.640 align:start position:19%
lifts off the ground. A jellyfish that
grows its own crops.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:32.280 align:start position:19%
Nature keeps surprising us.
Hit subscribe for more strange tales.

